 it so that if the length for the stored delta/doubleDelta is somehow corrupted to be too small, the attempt to unmarshal will return an error.\n\nThe current (broken) behavior is to return a malformed chunk, which can then lead to a panic when there is an attempt to read header values.\n\nThe referenced issue proposed creating chunks with a minimum length -- I instead opted to just error on the attempt to unmarshal, since I'm not clear on how it could be safe to proceed when the length is incorrect/unknown.\n\nThe issue also talked about possibly \"quarantining series\", but I don't know the surrounding code well enough to understand how to make that happen.\n\n(Also, in case you're wondering: I'm poking around in Prometheus as a way to brush up on my Go skills)\n\n@beorn7 \n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/prometheus/issues/1923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/prometheus/issues/1923/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":770888174,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDc3MDg4ODE3NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/prometheus/issues/events/770888174","actor":{"login":"dmilstein","id":658499,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODQ5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/658499?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein","html_url":"https://github.com/dmilstein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmilstein/orgs","repos_url":"https